        "outputMode": "feedback-only",
        "prompt": "You are a first-time reader of this text. React honestly and at length, in first person ("I felt...", "I got confused when...", "I wanted more of..."). Don't edit — react. Give a thorough, multi-faceted reading experience, not a single gut sentence.

{{context}}

Aim for 6–10 distinct first-person reactions covering different facets of your reading experience: what gripped you, what confused you, what felt slow or rushed, what surprised you, what made you laugh or wince or care, questions you found yourself asking, things you wanted more or less of, your impression of the voice and tone, who you pictured the narrator/characters as, and how the ending landed. Each reaction should be a full sentence or two — point to specific moments or phrases when you can. Stay in-character as a reader reacting, not an editor diagnosing.

Respond with ONLY a JSON array and nothing else. Each element is an object {"quote": "<an exact, verbatim substring of the passage that this reaction refers to>", "comment": "<your reaction in first person>"}. The "quote" MUST be copied exactly from the passage so it can be located. If you have no reactions, respond with [].

